ary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[35,36],"#Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[37,39],"#Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[38,39],"#Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[40,42],"#Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[41,42],"#Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[43,44]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/982CJF8J","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/I5C578VR?page=1&annotation=93CNVPKQ","line":35},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/I5C578VR?page=1&annotation=WYBGSQAQ","line":35},{"title":"Sayfa 4","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/I5C578VR?page=4&annotation=9LJEHJW8","line":38},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/I5C578VR?page=1&annotation=MF4CEUIX","line":41},{"title":"Sayfa 5","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/I5C578VR?page=5&annotation=3VA8M6QZ","line":41}],"metadata":{"Title":"Exploring the Potential of an AI Chatbot as a Supplementary Tool for Nutritional Prescription Hospital Discharge: A Preliminary Study","Authors":"Renato Augusto Da Cruz Pereira, Raianne Rodrigues Lima, Amanda Cristina Araujo Gomes, Fernanda Araújo Santos Saldanha, Dino Schwingel, Paulo Adriano Schwingel, Bruno Bavaresco Gambassi","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1155/sci5/2632410","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"Tis preliminary study evaluated the performance of a prominent AI chatbot in producing clinically valid nutritional guidelines. A specialist committee of registered dietitians selected 16 common medical and surgical pathologies. Standardized prompts were used to generate nutritional discharge guidelines from the chatboTe same committee then evaluated the AI-generated texts for technical accuracy and content presentation on a 0–10 scale (approval score ≥ 7.0).  Inter-rater reliability was assessed using the intraclass correlation coefcient (ICC) and Cohen’s Kappa","Findings":"Te evaluation of nutritional prescriptions generated by Google’s AI chatbot revealed varied performance across the 16 selected pathologies. Among these, eight (50.0%) achieved the minimum approval score of 7.0 or higher and were classifed as “Approved","Conclusions":"1.4), although this diference was not statistically signifcant (p > 0.05). Inter-rater reliability was substantial (ICC>0.72; Kappa>0.62). Te fndings indicate that AI chatbots hold promise as supplementary tools for drafting nutritional discharge summaries, potentially reducing administrative workload. However, their variable performance underscores the indispensable need for rigorous review and validation by qualifed healthcare professionals before any clinical applicatiTis study provides compelling preliminary evidence that a generative AI chatbot can serve as a valuable supplementary tool in producing structured and technically sound nutritional discharge prescriptions.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"prompt örnekleri var  klinisyen değ var"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1tntwe2","at":1774939760236},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/dacruzpereiraExploringPotentialAI2025b.md"},
